{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"count\" expr=\"0\"/>\n    <data id=\"done\" expr=\"false\"/>\n    <data id=\"user\" expr=\"({name:'bob'})\"/>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <transition event=\"go\" cond=\"In(b)\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml058-in-unquoted-state-id.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml058-in-unquoted-state-id.scxml"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":1,"byteOffset":290,"endColumn":38,"endLine":8,"startColumn":37,"startLine":8},"insertedContent":{"text":"'b'"}}]}],"description":{"text":"quote the state ID `'b'`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml058-in-unquoted-state-id.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":8,"startColumn":37,"startLine":8}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`In(b)` passes `b` unquoted, not the state ID `'b'`\n\n**Note:** in ECMAScript, `b` is a variable reference, not the state ID (no `<data id=\"b\">` declares it, so evaluating it raises `error.execution` unless a script defines it); `In()` takes the state ID as a string\n\n**Help:** quote the state ID: `In('b')`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions","text":"`In(b)` passes `b` unquoted, not the state ID `'b'`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":291,"start":290},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"in this `cond` on `<transition>`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml058-in-unquoted-state-id.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":39,"endLine":8,"startColumn":34,"startLine":8}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML058"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`In(stateID)` is true only while a `<state>`, `<parallel>`, or `<final>` with that ID is active, so a literal ID that names no state (usually a typo) makes the condition always false; in the ECMAScript and XPath data models an unquoted ID is a variable or a relative path, not the ID"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: name an existing state ID (the finding suggests the nearest one), and quote it as a string: `In('s1')`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML058` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#ConditionalExpressions","id":"SCXML058","name":"SCXML058","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an `In()` condition names no state of the machine or passes the state ID unquoted"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}